les with the number of transitions in the sequence by a fitted power: `beta · ((n−1)/5)^lam`, where `lam` has a Normal(0, 1) prior. When `lam` is 0 the model is the same as the current best one.\n\n**Why:** the strongest problem the critique found, and the only one that holds up after correcting for multiple tests (q = 0.048), is about sequence length. The current best model gets wrong how the preference for the sequence with more switches changes as sequences get longer. Letting sensitivity depend on length targets that directly. The idea is that a switch rate seen over a long sequence counts as stronger (or weaker) evidence than the same rate in a short one.\n\n- **Name:** `length_scaled_alternation_ideal`\n- **Smoke fit:** ELPD-LOO of −1069.6, against the current best model's −1072.0. That is a short single-chain run, so it's only a rough sign.\n- **Not yet verified:**\n  - **Convergence:** a single chain gives no R-hat.\n  - **LOO reliability:** the smoke fit's PSIS-LOO estimate was flagged as unreliable, with 3.3% of trials above the Pareto-k threshold against a 1% tolerance.\n  - **Novelty:** this only passes if the fitted `lam` is far enough from 0 to change predictions noticeably. If it isn't, the model will be rejected as a near-copy of the current best one.\n\nFiles are in `/scratch/users/kushinm/auto-psych/outer_loop_live/run2/data/subjective_randomness/experiment1/model_loop/iter_2/candidate_3/`:\n- `hypothesis.md`\n- `model_name.txt`\n- `candidate.py`","ttft_ms":4051,"type":"result","duration_ms":258262,"uuid":"1731a09f-2ceb-4b08-9a96-bf27423d17fa","ttft_stream_ms":2663,"time_to_request_ms":113,"first_content_frame_ms":2664,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0}
